<article class="env-lemma" id="04FV">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04FV">Lemma <span data-tag="04FV">59.46.1</span>.</a> Let $i : Z \to X$ be a closed immersion of schemes. Let $U, U'$ be schemes étale over $X$. Let $h : U_ Z \to U'_ Z$ be a morphism over $Z$. Then there exists a diagram </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ U &  W \ar[l]_ a \ar[r]^ b &  U' }  \]
</div>
  <p> in $X_{\acute{e}tale}$ such that $a_ Z : W_ Z \to U_ Z$ is an isomorphism and $h = b_ Z \circ (a_ Z)^{-1}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Consider the scheme $M = U \times _ X U'$. The graph $\Gamma _ h \subset M_ Z$ of $h$ is open. This is true for example as $\Gamma _ h$ is the image of a section of the étale morphism $\text{pr}_{1, Z} : M_ Z \to U_ Z$, see Étale Morphisms, Proposition <a href="/tag/024T" data-tag="024T">41.6.1</a>. Hence there exists an open subscheme $W \subset M$ whose intersection with the closed subset $M_ Z$ is $\Gamma _ h$. Set $a = \text{pr}_1|_ W$ and $b = \text{pr}_2|_ W$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>